tags: pages
title: "Contact Finding Balance Counseling | Austin, Texas"
description: Request a free consult for therapy, LPC supervision or EMDR consultation with Reem Glasco, LPC-S, in Austin, Texas. Online across the state.
nav: Contact
order: 12
---
<section class="shell band">
  <h1>Contact us</h1>
  {#- Outside .answer on purpose: the direct-answer passage should still open
      on how to reach the practice, not on how it feels to try. -#}
  <p class="hero-lede">Writing the first email is usually the hardest part of this, and it
  does not have to be good.</p>
  <div class="answer">
    <p>Email is the fastest route into the practice. Therapy consults are fifteen minutes,
    supervision and EMDR consultation consults are thirty, and both are free and commit you to
    nothing. Say briefly what you are looking for and when you are usually free; you will get
    times back, normally within a couple of working days.</p>
  </div>
  {#- The page every "Contact us" on the site points at had no button on it.
      Two routes, because some people would rather be prompted than face a
      blank email. -#}
  <div class="cta-row">
    <a class="cta" href="/contact/appointment/">Use the request form</a>
    <a class="cta cta--quiet" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">Email us directly</a>
  </div>

  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <h2>Reach the practice</h2>
      <dl class="facts">
        <div><dt>Email</dt><dd><a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a><span class="cell-note">Therapy, supervision and consultation all arrive here.</span></dd></div>
        {%- if site.phone %}
        <div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><a href="tel:{{ site.phone | replace(" ", "") | replace("(", "") | replace(")", "") | replace("-", "") }}">{{ site.phone }}</a></dd></div>
        {%- endif %}
        <div><dt>Based in</dt><dd>Austin, Texas</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Serving</dt><dd>Austin and all of Texas online</dd></div>
        <div><dt>In person</dt><dd>Trail walk sessions in central Texas; equine sessions in Dripping Springs</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Hours</dt><dd>By appointment; walk and talk therapy on Fridays</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Reply time</dt><dd>Usually a couple of working days</dd></div>
        {%- for p in site.profiles %}
        <div><dt>Directory</dt><dd><a href="{{ p.url }}">{{ p.name }} profile</a></dd></div>
        {%- endfor %}
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>What to include</h3>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li>Whether you want therapy, LPC supervision or EMDR consultation.</li>
        <li>Online or in person, and roughly where in Texas you are.</li>
        <li>Two or three windows of time that usually work for you.</li>
        <li>For supervision: your CV or resume, three professional references, and your answers
        to the <a href="/for-therapists/lpc-supervision/">application questions</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note">Nothing clinical, please. Ordinary email is not a secure channel, and a
      sentence about what you are looking for is all that is needed to get a consult booked.</p>

      <h3>Booking an associate instead</h3>
      <p>The practice's <a href="/therapy/associates/">LPC Associates</a> each run their own
      scheduling, and each one has a direct email and phone number on their card. Writing to
      them is faster than coming through here.</p>

      <h3>Already a client?</h3>
      <p><a href="/contact/forms/">Client forms</a>, including the Limits of Confidentiality
      notice and your Good Faith Estimate.</p>

      <h3>If this is urgent</h3>
      <p>This practice does not provide emergency care. Call 911 if you are in immediate
      danger, or call or text 988 for the Suicide and Crisis Lifeline.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
